Left over from k297 (apply worker, 2026-10-31): k297 makes a dev-mode dry run write nothing. In secure mode it still does: on a clone that has keys.yaml and age.key.enc but no .ocp/age.key, `ocp apply --dry-run` asks for PIN1 and writes .ocp/age.key and .ocp/age.pub before it stops.

Chosen fix (main, 2026-10-31 -- k297's own done criterion allows "works with the key in memory"): unlock the age key in memory only during a dry run -- OCP::Keys / OCP::Secrets accept an in-memory key instead of reading .ocp/age.key -- so the dry run still checks PIN1 and writes nothing. The alternative (skip PIN1/PIN2 in a dry run, apply lane) was not taken: the dry run would then no longer tell a wrong PIN before the real run.

Lanes: ocp-secrets-worker (in-memory unlock), then ocp-apply-worker (the dry-run call). Done = t/297's directory check extended to a secure-mode fixture (PIN via --pins-stdin): the project dir byte-for-byte unchanged, a wrong PIN1 still refused.

